  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Individual Measure to Strengthen the Response Capacity to Manage Migration Flows in Bosnia and Herzegovina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project builds on the three phases of the EU Special Measures to Support the Response to the Refugee and Migrant Situation in Bosnia and Herzegovina. Since 2017, mixed migratory flows have increased significantly in the Western Balkans. Comprised of a diverse group of people including asylum-seekers, refugees and migrants in search of a better life, mixed migratory flows in the Western Balkans and along the Eastern Mediterranean Route (EMR) constituted approximately 16% of all entries into the European Union (EU) in 2021. This Individual measure is being implemented over the course of three years with the overall objective to transition to sustainable, locally-, and state-owned mixed migration response and management. The first two years of the action serve as a transition phase during which capacity building is taking place while progressively transferring responsibilities to the state.</narrative>
  </description>
